# Safety Perf CAPA — Wave 1 (v2.66.19)

Locks the three fixes that closed the "load every incident into the
browser" path introduced during yesterday's Safety work.

## Invariants (do not regress)

1. `useSafetyIncidents()` (the unparameterised list overload in
   `src/hooks/useSafetyIncidents.ts`) is **deprecated** and ships with
   `enabled: false`. Do not re-enable it. Do not add new call sites.
   It exists only as a no-throw shim for one release.

2. SafetyHome's At-Risk queue (`SafetySlaQueueCard`) MUST use
   `useSafetySlaQueue()`. That hook is the only sanctioned source for
   the dashboard SLA tile and is bound to a server-side predicate:
   `status NOT IN (closed, orphaned) AND sla_state IN (red, amber)`,
   ordered by `sla_due_at ASC`, capped at 100 rows via `.range(0, 99)`.

3. Safety Analytics KPI drill-down (`KpiDrillDownDialog`) MUST use
   `useSafetyIncidentsByDrillKey(kind, open)`. The query is enabled only
   when the dialog is open AND a `kind` is set. Each kind maps to a
   server-side predicate (`open` → not in closed/orphaned; `closed` →
   status=closed; `critical` → severity=critical). Capped at 100 rows.

4. `SafetyIncidents.tsx → fetchIncidentsPage` MUST gate the `profiles`
   IN-query on `filters.typeName` matching `/accident/i`. Carrying the
   resolved `typeName` snapshot on the submitted filter object is the
   sanctioned pattern — do not re-introduce an unconditional join.

5. The legacy `useSafetyAssets(filters)` list hook (`select('*').limit(1000)`
   + in-memory `calibrationBucket` filter) is **deleted**. The
   `SafetyAssets` page is the only allowed list surface for assets and
   already pushes the bucket filter into a server-side date predicate
   via `useManualQuery`.

## Why

Pre-CAPA, SafetyHome mounted `useSafetyIncidents()` which issued a
`select('*')` against `safety_incidents_with_sla` with no `.range()`.
SafetySlaQueueCard + KpiDrillDownDialog then filtered the full result
set in-memory. Audit (sub-agent, 2026-06-12) classified this as 3
High-severity §113/ADR-050 violations.

## Out of scope (tracked separately)
- Wave 2: scoped mutation invalidations, severity-reorder RPC, Permits
  primitives swap, Training hardcoded `.limit()` migration, scoped
  SafetyHome realtime subscription.
- Wave 3: preventive `select('*')` tightening on reference tables.

